From 602d5286e5b344babe3050be6d3cca5185747c70 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rime-fork <rime-fork@localhost>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 09:48:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 27/28] Tell penglai_space the text around the caret before a
 space after text from elsewhere
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

With penglai_space/foreign on, penglai_space also guesses punctuation for a space pressed after text Sable never
sent (pasted, dictated, already in the document), from the sentence around the caret: "，" or "？" in a mostly
Chinese sentence, ", " in a mostly English one, a plain space when the character before the caret is not a letter,
digit or Han character.

The processor announces the setting by setting the property "penglai_space_foreign" to its schema id. Before a plain
space with nothing being composed in Chinese mode, only if that matches the current schema, read up to 100 UTF-16
units before and after the caret and put them in "penglai_space_before" and "penglai_space_after" (empty when the
client can't report its text, the caret is unknown, text is selected, the answer has an unexpected length, or the
text after the caret can't be read). length() can be expensive: it is called only when the client answers nil for a
range after the caret running past the end, to ask again within it. A length short of the caret (T3, an Electron app,
answers 0) is not used: nil for one unit after the caret means nothing is there; when one unit comes back, the client
keeps only part of the range, so take the actual range stringFromRange reports, or search for the longest length the
client gives (growing from 2, then halving; a miss is tried one unit longer, as a range ending inside a surrogate pair may
come back nil), instead of dropping the text before the caret.

The processor marks that space "foreign" instead of "punct": the units before the caret are checked against the text
just sent for this space instead of the last commit. A Return right after a guessed ", " turns it into "." the same
checked way a "，" becomes "。".
---
 sources/SquirrelInputController.swift | 114 +++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 112 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

